  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## The recordings\n\n- **dc2018-08-25.dc2018-08-25.vm44** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 176 min [1]\n- **deadco2018-08-25**: source not stated; 19 songs; 169 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [3]. Said about its sound: Very good for an audience recording; it almost sounds like a soundboard [4]\n- **dac2018-08-25.AKGmix.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 18 songs; 173 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer watched the show as part of a couch tour, across all four sets of the two shows [4]\n- Reviewer felt Dead & Company were starting to gel, with Mayer and Chimenti looking comfortable [4]\n- Reviewer says earlier years' performances, mostly because of tempo, kept them from letting go; this summer the band finally broke through [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dc2018-08-25.dc2018-08-25.vm44**: Recorded with Milab VM-44 microphones via S-Cards into a Sonosax SX-R4 at 24-bit/48kHz; Transfer: Sonosax to Audacity at 16/44, then CD Wave, then FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2018-08-25**: taped by Alex Leary; transferred by Alex Leary; source: DPA 4023 > Sound Devices MixPre-6 (24/48) [3]\n- **dac2018-08-25.AKGmix.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: OTS - back left corner of board, stand at about 10 feet > 2x AKG 391 cardioids ORTF and 2x AKG 393 hypercardioids pointed at stacks > Zoom F8 @44.1kHz/16-bit… [2]",
